---
import ClaimLedger from "../components/ClaimLedger.astro";
import RecalledSearchWorkbench from "../components/RecalledSearchWorkbench.astro";
import ResearchLayout from "../layouts/ResearchLayout.astro";
import data from "../generated/site-data.json";

const { authors, claims, links, licenses, packages, project, release, results } = data;
const authorNames = authors.map((author) => author.name).join(", ");
const shopify = results.shopify_global_catalog;
const ucp = results.ucp_direct_panels;
const visibleClaims = claims.filter((claim) => claim.site_visible);
const studyRows = shopify.cost_results ?? [];
---

<ResearchLayout title={project.title} description={project.abstract}>
  <header class="topbar">
    <div class="journal-mark">
      <a class="wordmark" href="#top" aria-label={`${project.title}, back to top`}>{project.slug}</a>
      <span>Research evidence release</span>
    </div>
    <nav aria-label="Primary navigation">
      <a href="#model">Model</a>
      <a href="#results">Results</a>
      <a href="#sources">Sources</a>
      <a href="#claims">Claims</a>
    </nav>
  </header>

  <main id="top">
    <section class="hero" aria-labelledby="paper-title">
      <div class="hero__content">
        <div class="article-kicker">
          <span>Computational research</span>
          <span>Version {release.version}</span>
          <span>Exploratory analysis</span>
        </div>
        <h1 id="paper-title">{project.title}</h1>
        <p class="subtitle">{project.subtitle}</p>
        <p class="hero-result">
          <span>Primary result</span>
          <strong>Use math to search again only when the expected saving can repay the next inspection cost.</strong>
        </p>
        <p class="collection-status">
          <span>Study status</span>
          Two complementary datasets make the decision measurable. Shopify seller decks quantify the value of another
          reveal inside an observed product graph; UCP direct-merchant panels characterize the wider search surface
          an agent may choose to enter.
        </p>
        <div class="author-block">
          <p class="byline">{authorNames}</p>
        </div>
        <div class="abstract-block">
          <p class="abstract-label">Abstract</p>
          <p class="abstract">{project.abstract}</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section section--rule" id="model" aria-labelledby="model-title">
      <div class="section__heading">
        <p class="section-number">1</p>
        <div><span class="eyebrow">Decision model</span><h2 id="model-title">Is another merchant inspection worth its cost?</h2></div>
      </div>
      <div class="prose">
        <p>A seller card reveals a price. The agent keeps its best observed offer and either buys it or pays to inspect another feasible card.</p>
        <div class="equation"><p aria-label="Search when expected retained-price improvement exceeds inspection cost">search iff E[max(best retained price minus next price, 0)] &gt; inspection cost</p></div>
        <p>With free recall and zero inspection cost, every feasible card should be opened. The inspection-cost grid is therefore a declared sensitivity analysis, not measured Shopify billing.</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section" id="results" aria-labelledby="results-title">
      <div class="section__heading">
        <p class="section-number">2</p>
        <div><span class="eyebrow">Held-out results</span><h2 id="results-title">Know when extra search earns its cost</h2></div>
      </div>
      <p class="section-intro">The held-out comparison is adaptive stopping versus costed search-all. At material inspection costs, adaptive stopping lowers total acquisition cost by avoiding remaining searches whose expected saving cannot repay them. At zero cost, search-all is reliably better; two small positive-cost sensitivity levels are inconclusive.</p>
      <div class="exact-table-wrap" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label="Held-out search policy evaluation results by inspection cost scenario">
        <table class="decision-table">
          <thead><tr><th>Cost</th><th>Comparator</th><th>Difference</th><th>95% interval</th><th>Products</th><th>Status</th></tr></thead>
          <tbody>
            {studyRows.map((row) => (
              <tr><td>${row.inspection_cost_usd.toFixed(2)}</td><td>search all</td><td>{row.adaptive_vs_search_all.mean_difference.toFixed(4)}</td><td>[{row.adaptive_vs_search_all.ci_lower.toFixed(4)}, {row.adaptive_vs_search_all.ci_upper.toFixed(4)}]</td><td>{row.adaptive_vs_search_all.product_clusters}</td><td>{row.adaptive_vs_search_all.favors_treatment ? "Adaptive improvement" : row.adaptive_vs_search_all.ci_lower > 0 ? "Search-all improvement" : "No reliable improvement"}</td></tr>
            ))}
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
      <RecalledSearchWorkbench />
    </section>

    <section class="section" id="sources" aria-labelledby="sources-title">
      <div class="section__heading">
        <p class="section-number">3</p>
        <div><span class="eyebrow">Evidence design</span><h2 id="sources-title">Two sources, separate roles</h2></div>
      </div>
      <div class="prose-grid">
        <div class="prose"><h3>Shopify Global Catalog</h3><p>{shopify.product_deck_count} title-normalized USD seller decks and {shopify.seller_card_count} seller cards support the held-out study: {shopify.calibration_product_count} decks calibrate policies and {shopify.held_out_product_count} product clusters are held out. The evidence is a recovered complete prefix of {shopify.completed_query_count} of {shopify.planned_query_count} registered deep queries. Title identity was revised after collection, and shop domains do not prove independent companies or checkout equivalence.</p></div>
        <div class="prose"><h3>UCP Direct Merchant Panels</h3><p>{ucp.included_lifecycle_dates.length} lifecycle dates are retained, while {Object.keys(ucp.excluded_dates).length} common-mode discontinuity is excluded. These observations document catalog surface quality, not Pandora policy performance.</p></div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section" id="claims" aria-labelledby="claims-title">
      <div class="section__heading">
        <p class="section-number">4</p>
        <div><span class="eyebrow">Executable ledger</span><h2 id="claims-title">Claims stay tied to evidence</h2></div>
      </div>
      <ClaimLedger claims={visibleClaims} />
    </section>

    <section class="section" aria-labelledby="materials-title">
      <div class="section__heading">
        <p class="section-number">5</p>
        <div><span class="eyebrow">Materials</span><h2 id="materials-title">Reproducible collection and replay</h2></div>
      </div>
      <dl class="artifact-list">
        <div><dt>Repository</dt><dd><a href={links.repository}>Source and generated artifacts</a></dd></div>
        <div><dt>Python</dt><dd>{packages.python.distribution}</dd></div>
        <div><dt>JavaScript</dt><dd>{packages.javascript.name}</dd></div>
        <div><dt>Licenses</dt><dd>{licenses.code} · {licenses.content}</dd></div>
      </dl>
    </section>
  </main>

  <footer><div><p class="footer-title">{project.title}</p><p>{authorNames} · Version {release.version}</p></div><p><a href={links.repository}>Repository</a></p></footer>
</ResearchLayout>